# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# Item 738 (steps/capture-738.md; Q38/Q42/Q44): the host `makeReader` declares `loc: merge: Model`, writes
# `loc\value`, and returns the model `read`, which reads `loc\value`.  The node carries a copy of the
# fields the model reads -- `value` alone, not `other` or `box` (Q42 p. 2) -- and `loc\value` is read by
# Model's slot through the copy's table in the arena's `implements` table (D-105).  `box` is a Structure
# field the model does not read: the capture copies value cells only, so a copy of every field would be
# refused at the return.  The base translator refused the host: "a callable merge needs a walkable
# body".  Success is 7.
Inner:
    int: c 5
end: Inner

Model:
    int: other 5
    box:
        int: c 5
    int: value 0
end: Model

fn: makeReader (int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    loc: merge: Model
    loc\value: n
    fn: read (int: x) int
        return: loc\value + x
    return: read

@: r40 makeReader(40)
@: r7 makeReader(7)
int: a (r40: 2)
int: b (r7: 2)
int: ok 7
if: a != 42
    ok: 1
if: b != 9
    ok: 2
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
